Subject: [PATCH] Do not strand BTM reports behind completed AP capability state

A client can roam while its agent radio remains in AP-capability-report
state. BTM reports waited there until their ten-second command TTL, reserving
the radio and delaying already completed candidate replies beyond the HTTP
measurement deadline. Admit the existing report transaction in that state.
Restore it on the matching report ACK, and require the report MID to be
cleared before releasing the radio. Wrong ACKs and failed sends do not
complete the transaction. Earlier onboarding states remain gated.

Reporting periods, report retry behavior and timeout budgets are unchanged.

Upstream-Status: Pending

--- a/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
+++ b/src/orch/em_orch_agent.cpp
@@ -288,8 +288,10 @@
             break;
 
         case em_cmd_type_btm_report:
-            if ((em->get_state() == em_state_agent_configured) ||
-                (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_topo_synchronized)) {
+            if (em->get_btm_report_msg_id() == 0 &&
+                ((em->get_state() == em_state_agent_configured) ||
+                 (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_topo_synchronized) ||
+                 (em->get_state() == em_state_agent_ap_cap_report))) {
                 return true;
             }
             break;
@@ -346,7 +348,8 @@
